ns.guideText = {
  ["forever.warrior"] = "Stances change what you can press. Battle Stance is yours at level 1, Defensive Stance at 10 and Berserker Stance at 30, both from quests. Rage comes from hitting and from being hit, a critical hit gives more of it, and it drains when you stop. Every line below presses a button.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.dry"] = "Rage you put into Heroic Strike is rage your next Mortal Strike will not have.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.intro"] = "Arms hits slowly and hard with one big weapon. If you carry a two-hander, this is your tree. Sweeping Strikes at 30 and Mortal Strike at 40 are what the first 40 points are for.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.line"] = "A two-hander, Sweeping Strikes and Mortal Strike. The build for groups and for chains of monsters.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.note"] = "(31 points in Arms for Mortal Strike, then 20 in Fury and Arms.)",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p1"] = "Rend bleeds for more, and Deep Wounds needs this at full rank. It is also the Rend that Bloodthrill looks for later.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p10"] = "Your critical hits do more damage. It needs Deep Wounds at full rank.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p11"] = "Your next 5 melee attacks hit a second monster nearby. This is why Arms is the group build, and Mortal Strike needs it.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p12"] = "Your main-hand hits on a monster with your Rend on it can give a free Overpower. Keep Rend on the monster to use it.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p13"] = "Your critical hits do more damage. It needs Deep Wounds at full rank.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p14"] = "A bonus for the weapon you hold: critical chance for an axe or polearm, armour ignored for a mace or staff, an extra attack now and then for a sword.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p15"] = "Slam stops stalling your swing, and comes back sooner. Do not press Slam without it.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p16"] = "A bonus for the weapon you hold: critical chance for an axe or polearm, armour ignored for a mace or staff, an extra attack now and then for a sword.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p17"] = "Your hardest hit, and it halves the healing the monster gets. It needs Sweeping Strikes and 30 points in Arms, so level 40 exactly.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p18"] = "Slam stops stalling your swing, and comes back sooner. Do not press Slam without it.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p19"] = "Melee critical hits come more often, and a critical hit gives you extra rage. The last points go to Fury.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p2"] = "Each rank adds parry. One guide says a parry speeds up your next swing, which makes it a strong levelling stat.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p20"] = "A hit may give you 1 more rage. It is small, but it is rage on every swing you make.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p21"] = "Being hit can make you hit harder for a while. One guide says it is the better pick outdoors and in dungeons.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p22"] = "Your next 4 melee attacks give 5 more rage each. Check its tooltip for the cost, because the game's table and a guide disagree.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p23"] = "Slows every monster close to you, so a chase ends your way. Take it for the pull that goes wrong.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p24"] = "Your rage decays later once the fight is over, so the next pull starts with some.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p3"] = "Overpower crits far more often, and it cannot be dodged, blocked or parried. It is your answer to a monster that dodges.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p4"] = "Charge gives more rage, so the first hit of every fight starts with something to spend.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p5"] = "Each rank adds parry. One guide says a parry speeds up your next swing, which makes it a strong levelling stat.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p6"] = "A critical hit makes the monster bleed on top of the damage. It needs Improved Rend at full rank, and Impale needs this.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p7"] = "Each rank adds parry. One guide says a parry speeds up your next swing, which makes it a strong levelling stat.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p8"] = "An extra attack that hits Giants, Dragonkin and mounted targets much harder, and knocks riders off. Skip it if you never meet them.",
  ["forever.warrior-arms.p9"] = "Each rank adds damage to every hit with a two-hander. It is small, but it is on every swing you make.",
