  ["forever.warrior-arms.split"] = "the last 20 points and the order of Bloodthrill and Weaponmaster. Mobalytics takes Bloodthrill first, then all of Weaponmaster, then Fury. Warcraft Tavern would put Bloodthrill first and Weaponmaster as an equal pick. Enrage is the pick this page makes, and Mobalytics names Lingering Rage as the other.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.dry"] = "A fight you win without Death Wish is a fight you did not need it for.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.intro"] = "Fury hits fast with a weapon in each hand and lives on critical hits and rage. It is weak until about level 36, strong after, and slower than Protection. Use your best weapon until you learn to dual wield at 20.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.line"] = "Two weapons, critical hits and rage. Weak until about 36, then a fast grinder of single monsters.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.note"] = "(31 points in Fury for Bloodthirst, then the rest in Fury, with 5 in Arms last.)",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p1"] = "Melee critical hits come more often, and a critical hit gives you extra rage. Every Fury order starts here.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p10"] = "Enrage, Berserker Rage, Bloodrage, Death Wish and Bloodthirst make your next 3 hits heal you. Long grinds need that.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p11"] = "Whirlwind comes back sooner and hits the closest monster harder.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p12"] = "Enrage, Berserker Rage, Bloodrage, Death Wish and Bloodthirst make your next 3 hits heal you. Long grinds need that.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p13"] = "A critical hit speeds up your next few swings. It has 3 ranks.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p14"] = "Your main attack from here: a hard hit that also makes you run faster for a while. It needs 30 points in Fury, so level 40 exactly.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p15"] = "A critical hit speeds up your next few swings. It has 3 ranks.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p16"] = "Your off-hand hits for more and gives more rage.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p17"] = "Whirlwind comes back sooner and hits the closest monster harder.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p18"] = "A hit may give you 1 more rage. It is small, but it is rage on every swing you make.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p19"] = "Your next 4 melee attacks give 5 more rage each. Check its tooltip for the cost, because the game's table and a guide disagree.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p2"] = "Your rage decays later once the fight is over, so a chain of pulls keeps its rage.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p20"] = "Execute costs less rage, so you can finish a monster sooner.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p21"] = "Slows every monster close to you, so a chase ends your way. Take it for the pull that goes wrong.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p22"] = "Spare points. Each rank adds a little parry.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p23"] = "Rend bleeds for more. It has nothing before it in Arms, so it is a cheap place for the last points.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p3"] = "Your off-hand hits miss less. Guides rank it among the best points of the build.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p4"] = "A big hit on you, or a critical, heals you over a few seconds. Gore Drinker needs it at full rank.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p5"] = "Being hit can make you hit harder for a while. Five points by level 30 is where Fury starts to feel strong.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p6"] = "More physical damage for a while, and you cannot be feared. You take more damage while it runs, so use it on a fight you can win.",
  ["forever.warrior-fury.p7"] = "Berserker Rage gives 10 rage on the spot and frees you from slows. It is also a button for Gore Drinker.",
